   "Both an absolute-address syntactic domain and a base-relative-offset syntactic domain are present; the latter has no base field in these arrays. Register-programming semantics and consumers are not established.",
   "No absolute table key reaches any of the four ranked MC bases; this is an absolute-table-key result only.",
   "The exact materialisation rows derive the precise bounded result: 0x00003333 and 0x00300014 have stored_word_total=0, zero exact one-instruction MOVZ/MOVN sites, zero exact adjacent MOVZ/MOVN-then-MOVK sites and zero ORR sites across all nine exact images. 0xc003ffff has 24 stored occurrences and 0x00111111 has 3; computed, loaded, differently ordered or otherwise unmodeled materialisation remains UNKNOWN."
  ],
  "REFUTED": [
   "An absolute-address table key in these exact DCB blocks reaches one of the four ranked MC bases."
  ],
  "SUPPORTED": [
   "The strict pair-array shapes support a candidate data-driven programming input hypothesis, but do not link an array to a register writer or assign an undocumented base/register meaning."
  ],
  "UNKNOWN": [
   "The implicit base of every base-relative table.",
   "Whether any ranked value is computed at runtime rather than stored, and whether a boot-time write is later changed; the section-7 live-value mismatch cannot exclude either sequence.",
   "Whether DDR training firmware outside these nine partitions writes them.",
   "Register-programming semantics, consumers, the relation to the Experiment 014 GF(2) bank relation, post-boot writability, alias and boundary bypass."
  ]
